00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.860
think Jacob's screen test
was his first time he ever

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.810
set foot on a set in his life.

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:29.670
And now to see how
far they've come

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.660
and have the end of
the trilogy here,

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.905
I'm very excited
to see the movie.

00:11:32.905 --> 00:11:33.705
I haven't seen it yet.

00:11:33.705 --> 00:11:37.320
I'm very excited to see it
and to see how the fans react.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:41.560
 Well, you've done an
incredible job at casting.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.990
Kudos to you.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.940
What was it like
bringing back characters

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.980
like William and Alfred?

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.460
 Am I allowed to
talk about that?

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.160
I don't think so, Meghan.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.140
 I mean, it was in the trailer.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.400
Come on, Sarah.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.510
I think you can.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:55.800
 Oh yeah.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.000
It's bonkers.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.580
This movie is as big as
anything we've ever done.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.060
And it's really exciting to
see how they're all going

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.530
to interact on screen together.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.930
 Did you ever think
that would happen?

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.550
 No, I didn't, I didn't.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:10.050
When I first heard the
idea for the movie,

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.430
I thought, this is impossible.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.750
But--

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.160
 But here we are.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.150
Here we are.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:16.335
OK.

00:12:16.335 --> 00:12:18.240
Was there a moment where
you're like, I don't

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.650
know if we can pull this off?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.850
This is so big.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:23.070
This is the biggest
Spider-Man film yet.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:26.070
 Yes, luckily on my
end, a lot of the cast

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.680
was already in existence
that I had cast

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.420
and from other wonderful
casting directors

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:33.310
who worked on this film
in much earlier versions.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.130
So in terms of
pulling it off, I'm

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.710
going to toss that ball to the
incredible production people,

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.470
our producers, Amy,
Rachel, Kevin Feige, Jon

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.810
Watts, everyone who
worked so hard to pull

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.070
off a movie on this scale.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:00.840
 Hi Marvel fans.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.655
I am here with Victoria
Alonso, executive producer.

00:13:03.655 --> 00:13:04.930
How are you doing?
- I'm great.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:05.730
I'm excited.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.050
Now Zendaya is coming.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.520
So that's the party right there.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.880
 We got a party
going on here too.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.350
 Yes, today is a good day.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.760
Today is a good day.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:19.650
We get to celebrate Spider-Man,
one of my favorite characters--

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.950
not the favorite,
but one of my--

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.690
 Nice save.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.130
 They're all my favorites.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.420
 Tonight is a big night.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:30.960
This is the biggest Spider-Man
film that we've seen to date.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:34.120
And the effects are on
a whole other level.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.640
Can you talk about
that just a little bit?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.830
Just there's just so
much that went into this.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.920
 You know, the thing about
working on these things,

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.840
it just feels--
during the pandemic,

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:47.490
this took far more effort
because we were not together.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:51.460
And I think that what I longed
for is to be together again.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.900
But we got it done
thanks to the 6,000-plus

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.500
people across the world.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.060
So I think every single
vendor, facility, human,

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.100
artist, and family
member that put

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.750
up with us working from home.

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.790
And hopefully you
can all go see it.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:11.230
And shh, keep the secrets.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.073
 I thought you were
going to tell us a secret.

00:14:13.073 --> 00:14:17.080
 Shh, I'll say-- no,
are you kidding me?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.940
I'm not saying anything.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.960
 OK, all right, all right.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.690
Well, what are you most excited
about with this film tonight?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:26.290
 I'm excited to see how
people react to something that

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.295
has been with us for so long.

00:14:29.295 --> 00:14:34.150
So I'm just ready, ready for
all of you to know what I know.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:37.570
 OK, well, I'm
ready for that, too.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.000
How did you and your
team pull this off?

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.220
 Well, you know, every
movie takes a lot of effort.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.700
So it just, it was
effort, effort, effort.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:46.690
And we have the best team.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:50.710
You know, Amy, Kevin, we have
Jon Watts who is fantastic,

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:55.540
and we have a beautiful trio
and Zendaya and Tom and Jake.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.500
And the friends are back.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.360
They're back in town.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:01.420
So they get to
tell another story.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.290
 That's beautiful.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.530
Well, what does this
night mean to you?

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:08.980
I hope that this gift of
filmmaking that we put out

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.260
there to the world is
received with as much love

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.840
as we made it.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.670
 That made my heart
feel like mushy.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:16.760
I love that.

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:17.710
I don't want to keep you.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.203
Enjoy the rest of
your red carpet.

00:15:19.203 --> 00:15:20.470
And I look forward
to seeing the film.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:21.740
 Thank you.
Thank you for your support.

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.380
And if I don't
see you anymore, I

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.940
think that's it for this year.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.410
We have nine projects
that came this year.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.600
Happy holidays.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.940
We represented with
all of our hearts.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:33.230
So we'll see you, after this,
we'll see you next year.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:34.030
 All right, see you.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:34.830
Thank you.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:50.800
 Hey Marvel fans.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:51.970
We're here with Amy Pascal.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.980
This is an incredible movie.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.440
What does it feel like to get
this off the ground running?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.360
 Look, it's fantastic.

00:15:58.360 --> 00:15:59.350
People are out.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.610
People are excited.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.090
People love Spider-Man.

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:02.890
It's great.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.930
 So Spider-Man, talking
about the love of Spider-Man,

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.080
he's so relatable.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:08.110
What makes Spider-Man
so beloved by all?

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.760
 I think because
Spider-Man means

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.620
something different to
everyone at different

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.180
ages in their life.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.730
You know, when you're a little
kid, it means one thing.

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:17.590
When you're a teenager,
something else.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.900
And when you're grown
up, something else.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:21.970
You know, it's a
boy who's always

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:24.680
struggling with being good.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.950
And I think we all
understand that.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:29.110
 We were able to bring the
super villains from previous

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:31.060
Spider-Man into this film.

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:32.560
What was that process like that?

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.690
 It was fantastic
because, of course,

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:37.960
I had worked with all of
them on the other films.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.190
And it was really exciting
to bring them back.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:41.750
 Out of your entire
Spider-Man journey,

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.450
what are you most proud of?

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.430
 Tonight, of course.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.270
 I love it.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.800
Amy, thank you so much.
Enjoy the movie.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.640
Thank you so much.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:04.770
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:07.560
We're here with Jon Watts,
the director, and family.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.690
So Jon is an incredibly
incredible director.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.310
We've seen two Spider-Man
movies already.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.800
What makes him so amazing?

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.230
 That's intense.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:17.069
 Well, he's our brother.

00:17:17.069 --> 00:17:19.410
 He's our baby brother,
yeah, he's the baby brother.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.200
 I wanted to bring my
family on the red carpet just

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.140
because, you know,
historically, Spider-Man is out

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.190
there helping regular people.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:27.990
That's what he does.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:30.840
And my family
literally does that.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.080
My brother is a firefighter.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:32.880
My sister is a nurse.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.040
My other sister
here is a teacher.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.630
And they're like
actually out there

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.690
on the front lines
legitimately helping

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:42.130
people over this past
terrible year and a half.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.120
So I just wanted to sort of take
a little bit of the spotlight

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.520
off of me and shine on them and
all the people that have been

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.950
doing great things to
help people in this really

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.240
tough couple of years.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:52.500
 That's amazing.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.470
That's incredible.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:54.270
 That's your answer.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.440
 That's your answer.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:58.710
 So Jon just spoke about
how you inspire him.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.380
How does he inspire you?

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.400
 Oh my goodness.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.520
 I bring them to
red carpet events.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.950
They get to meet Tom
Holland and Zendaya.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:11.820
 Now this is a huge, huge
film, where did you even begin?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.540
 Well, at the end
of the last movie,

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:18.930
we kind of gave ourselves
a really big ending where

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.400
we revealed Peter's identity.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:23.400
So we started there.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.600
 Straight to the
point, I love it.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.790
 Now super villains
from previous Spider-Man

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.915
movies are in this film.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.100
What was it like to
be a part of that?

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:33.900
 Oh, it was great.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.760
I mean, I'm a fan
of those movies.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.940
So to have them there,
I was just being

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.110
a nerd like everyone else.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.570
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:57.740
We're here with Simu Liu.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.790
What is going on?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:18:59.870
We're here at the live carpet.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:00.920
How does it feel?

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:01.740
 It feels pretty great.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.550
I'm not sure that
these people realize

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.380
that I'm not in this movie.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.827
I think they-- you
know, I'm not going

00:19:08.827 --> 00:19:09.860
to burst their bubble for them.

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:11.010
 No spoilers, no spoilers.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.080
 No spoilers at all.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.010
Anything is possible.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.800
But I'm also not in this movie.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:20.330
 So who are you most
excited to see in this film?

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.770
 I'm excited to see Spider-Man.

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:24.570
 No spoilers.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:29.900
 Whichever Spider-Mans--
question mark?

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:33.950
I'm excited to-- no, no, I mean,
I've been reading the rumors

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:35.000
like everybody else.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.060
I'm so fortunate to
get to be here to get

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:39.890
to watch this movie early.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:42.650
And I'm just excited to
see where they take it.

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.810
I've been such a fan of
the Spider-Man movies

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.460
ever since Tobey Maguire.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.430
I think it's just been a really
long ride and a full circle

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.540
moment for a lot of people.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.700
So I'm jazzed.

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:53.670
I'm excited.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:54.470
 Let's talk about that.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.780
Previous super villains
are in this movie.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:59.030
What was your reaction
when you found out?

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.410
 I was pretty--

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:03.470
OK, OK, well, first of all,
I was like oh my god, Doctor

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:04.760
Octopus is in the trailer.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.430
And then I was like,
oh my god, like Jamie

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.750
Foxx is there as Electro.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.760
And then it was like
oh my god, he's got

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:12.870
the Stark tech on his armor.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:14.750
So I was like, what
does that mean?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:15.950
I feel like everyone
was, you know,

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.420
pretty blown away
by all of that.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.860
I think, you know, I
work for this company

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.650
so I know people at Marvel.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.780
They're master marketers.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.340
They're mysterious.

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:26.870
They work in mysterious ways.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.940
They operate behind a veil
of secrecy and shadow.

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.010
And, you know, I'm just excited.

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:35.810
I'm so excited
that I finally get

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.900
to take a peek behind and see
what they've been cooking up.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.080
You know, I feel
like I deserve to be

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.510
here because I used
to play Spider-Man

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.410
at kids' birthday parties.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:47.210
I dressed up.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.900
I inhabited the character.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:52.280
You know, I was in the costume.

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:54.270
I really, I feel like
I was Spider-Man.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:57.260
So in a way, I do feel
like this is my premiere.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.760
 Could I still hire you for
birthdays or is it too late?

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:02.610
 You can, but the rate
is now $75,000 an hour.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:03.410
 Oh, no, Spider-Man.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.603
 It's gone up a
little bit, yes.

00:21:05.603 --> 00:21:06.770
 Thank you, Simu,
have a good one.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:07.570
Take it easy.

