I got an email from
Kevin Feige saying

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:41.310
it's fast becoming the WCU.

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:44.290
So I'll take that.

00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:45.480
So here we are.

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:47.880
 The Wong Cinematic
Universe, I like it.

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.010
I like it, definitely.

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:51.780
Well, what is it like
to get a chance to dive

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:55.800
into the Marvel multiverse with
all the weird creative worlds

00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:57.210
that it entails?

00:22:57.210 --> 00:23:02.220
 Well, we'll certainly have
to do a lot of versions.

00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:06.600
And it's also kind of filming
as well during this sort of time

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:09.540
as well where
we're kind of like,

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.260
you know, if something happens,
you know, then we hit plan B,

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:19.140
we hit plan C. So we're kind
of living in a sort of quantum

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:22.410
filming schedule, you know?

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:23.790
So that's how it's been.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.280
 That must be
crazy as an actor.

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:28.110
 Yeah, I mean I call
it like the madness

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:28.950
of the multi-schedule.

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:29.750
That's it, really.

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:31.170
You know, that's a strange that.

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.360
 Well, before you leave,
what's something that you can

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:35.010
tell us that the fans
can look forward to,

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:35.880
maybe a little tease?

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:42.000
 Well, you know,
there'll be a shift,

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:46.470
I think, definitely in
this which will hopefully,

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:50.740
you know, we'll see different
responsibilities I think,

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:51.540
you know?

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:08.870
 Marvel fans I'm here
with Marisa Tomei.

00:24:08.870 --> 00:24:09.920
How's it going?

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:12.620
 Going good, getting
very excited for everyone

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:13.550
to see this movie.

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.500
It's the big opening.

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:17.070
 The energy is amazing.

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:18.200
I'm so excited.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:20.780
 Yeah, it's very,
it's really thrilling.

00:24:20.780 --> 00:24:24.980
 What has May been up to
since we last left off?

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.360
 Well, her and Peter Parker
have gone through a lot

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:28.160
together.

00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:29.750
They're growing up.

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:32.090
They've been through
several cycles

00:24:32.090 --> 00:24:36.270
of on and off relationships
with other people.

00:24:36.270 --> 00:24:37.070
I don't know.

00:24:37.070 --> 00:24:38.810
They're hanging out.

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:40.730
 I mean, that's a lot.

00:24:40.730 --> 00:24:43.340
So everyone knows that
Peter Parker is Spider-Man.

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.290
How is May handling that?

00:24:45.290 --> 00:24:48.750
 I think that, well,
May was shocked at first.

00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:51.590
And then, you know,
then she found out.

00:24:51.590 --> 00:24:53.510
And they became a team.

00:24:53.510 --> 00:24:55.250
They just really
worked together.

00:24:55.250 --> 00:24:58.550
And she's in on it with him.

00:24:58.550 --> 00:25:00.320
And she also tries
to protect the part

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:03.440
of him that's still a boy
and lets him do his thing.

00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:04.500
 I love that.

00:25:04.500 --> 00:25:07.460
So and you just spilled
the tea, all right?

00:25:07.460 --> 00:25:10.520
May has a kind of a different
understanding when it comes

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:12.270
to her relationship with Happy.

00:25:14.930 --> 00:25:16.310
Is there a relationship there?

00:25:16.310 --> 00:25:17.490
What's going on?

00:25:17.490 --> 00:25:18.290
 I don't think--

00:25:18.290 --> 00:25:20.480
I mean, there's a relationship,
there's a friendship.

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:23.030
And they've also,
they're like compadres.

00:25:23.030 --> 00:25:24.600
They've been through
so much together.

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:26.060
They've been lovers.
They've been friends.

00:25:26.060 --> 00:25:27.440
They've been on.
They've been off.

00:25:27.440 --> 00:25:29.930
I don't know why you think
I have a different-- why?

00:25:29.930 --> 00:25:31.940
Do you have a different
understanding?

00:25:31.940 --> 00:25:33.530
 I mean, the last
movie, it was kind

00:25:33.530 --> 00:25:34.760
of like a little back and--

00:25:34.760 --> 00:25:38.125
 Oh, yeah, yes yes, yes, true.

00:25:38.125 --> 00:25:40.310
What was it like to work with
this incredible cast again?

00:25:40.310 --> 00:25:43.670
 Oh, it's just so
great to see them.

00:25:43.670 --> 00:25:45.860
They're always doing
something new and different

00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:47.630
and they just--

00:25:47.630 --> 00:25:48.433
they're so beautiful.

00:25:48.433 --> 00:25:49.400
They're beautiful to look at.

00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:50.540
They're beautiful inside.

00:25:50.540 --> 00:25:54.910
And it's always fun to come
back and be with them again.

00:25:54.910 --> 00:25:56.810
 Well, I'm excited to see
you on the big screen tonight.

00:25:56.810 --> 00:25:58.100
I won't keep you
from the red carpet.

00:25:58.100 --> 00:25:59.370
Thank you for
spending time with us.

00:25:59.370 --> 00:26:00.320
 Thanks, thanks to you.

00:26:15.820 --> 00:26:18.370
 Marvel fans, I am
joined by Xochitl Gomez.

00:26:18.370 --> 00:26:19.330
How's it going?

00:26:19.330 --> 00:26:20.460
 I'm doing great.

00:26:20.460 --> 00:26:21.260
I'm nervous.

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:22.490
I'm excited.

00:26:22.490 --> 00:26:24.340
 What are you looking
forward to seeing

00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:26.050
most in this film tonight?

00:26:26.050 --> 00:26:29.500
 Well, number one, my homies,
Benedict Cumberbatch and Benny

00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:32.050
Wong, got to support the crew.

00:26:32.050 --> 00:26:36.160
I'm really excited to see
just this movie in general.

00:26:36.160 --> 00:26:38.320
 Have you been a Spider-Man
fan for a long time?

00:26:38.320 --> 00:26:43.300
 Oh yeah, I'm like, who hasn't
been since like five years old,

00:26:43.300 --> 00:26:45.970
I mean, are you kidding me?

00:26:45.970 --> 00:26:46.870
 That makes sense.

00:26:46.870 --> 00:26:47.670
You're right.

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:49.870
So there's quite a bit of
crossover between the cast

00:26:49.870 --> 00:26:53.290
and the cast in your upcoming
film, Marvel Studios' Doctor

00:26:53.290 --> 00:26:55.360
Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness,

00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:57.820
what is it like
working with Benedict

00:26:57.820 --> 00:26:59.320
Cumberbatch and Benedict Wong?

00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:02.390
 Oh, I mean, it's
pretty insane.

00:27:02.390 --> 00:27:03.580
I'm a pretty lucky person.

00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:04.420
It's pretty crazy.

00:27:04.420 --> 00:27:07.210
I just love watching them get in
their character and their zone.

00:27:07.210 --> 00:27:10.480
And it's just been wonderful
like teaching experience,

00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:12.010
honestly.

00:27:12.010 --> 00:27:14.560
It's just crazy to be like, oh
my gosh, I know these people.

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:16.220
It's kind of funny.

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:17.020
 I bet.

00:27:17.020 --> 00:27:21.380
Who are you excited to see most
on this red carpet tonight?

00:27:21.380 --> 00:27:22.820
 Zendaya.

00:27:22.820 --> 00:27:23.620
Zendaya.

00:27:23.620 --> 00:27:24.670
 Girl, yes.

00:27:24.670 --> 00:27:25.510
 I'm excited.

00:27:25.510 --> 00:27:29.020
I'm like, I'm like,
is she here now?

00:27:29.020 --> 00:27:30.340
 I'm waiting for the screams.

00:27:30.340 --> 00:27:31.140
 I know.

00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:32.690
[CHEERING]

00:27:32.690 --> 00:27:34.655
 I hear some screams.

00:27:34.655 --> 00:27:36.497
Could be her.

00:27:36.497 --> 00:27:37.430
 So I heard you skateboard.

00:27:37.430 --> 00:27:38.230
Is that true?

00:27:38.230 --> 00:27:40.340
 Yes, I do a little
bit of skateboarding.

00:27:40.340 --> 00:27:42.590
But ever since I started
getting some roles,

00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:44.910
I was like, I can't
really injure myself here.

00:27:44.910 --> 00:27:48.350
So I just, I just
grazed a little bit.

00:27:48.350 --> 00:27:49.520
MEGHAN CAMARENA:
No crazy tricks.

00:27:49.520 --> 00:27:51.050
 No, no, no, no.

00:27:51.050 --> 00:27:53.210
I might be able to have
like some fake blood

00:27:53.210 --> 00:27:57.380
and stuff for work, but not
nothing in real life, nah.

00:27:57.380 --> 00:27:58.610
 That's a cool skill to have.

00:27:58.610 --> 00:28:00.470
And you just celebrated
your quinceñera?

00:28:00.470 --> 00:28:01.430
 Yes, I did.

00:28:01.430 --> 00:28:03.480
It was during COVID and stuff.

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:06.110
So I couldn't really have some
like huge thing, which, I mean,

00:28:06.110 --> 00:28:07.520
I really wish I could have.

00:28:07.520 --> 00:28:10.493
But I just went around the
park and around just LA

00:28:10.493 --> 00:28:11.360
and just took some photos.

00:28:27.370 --> 00:28:28.170
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:28:28.170 --> 00:28:30.080
We're here with Jacob
Batalon who plays Ned Leeds.

00:28:30.080 --> 00:28:31.610
This is a huge film.

00:28:31.610 --> 00:28:32.940
Where do we start
with Ned in this one?

00:28:32.940 --> 00:28:33.740
 Oh my goodness.

00:28:33.740 --> 00:28:34.540
Ned is reeling.

00:28:34.540 --> 00:28:36.050
You know, his best
friend's identity has just

00:28:36.050 --> 00:28:37.030
been revealed to the world.

00:28:37.030 --> 00:28:38.430
So he was just like,
what does he do next?

00:28:38.430 --> 00:28:39.650
What are we up to now?

00:28:39.650 --> 00:28:40.940
Like we're planning what to do.

00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:42.020
It's crazy.

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:43.850
 Does Ned to get on
the action on this one?

00:28:43.850 --> 00:28:46.010
 Oh my goodness, like
you wouldn't believe.

00:28:46.010 --> 00:28:48.140
Ned and MJ are killing it.

00:28:48.140 --> 00:28:49.760
 Yes, so what was
it like working

00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:50.870
with Benedict Cumberbatch?

00:28:50.870 --> 00:28:52.010
 I mean, unbelievable.

00:28:52.010 --> 00:28:53.660
He's like so
professional, but also

00:28:53.660 --> 00:28:55.610
such a funny,
amazing human being.

00:28:55.610 --> 00:28:57.890
And everyone on the
cast has been amazing.

00:28:57.890 --> 00:29:00.540
Every legend that's been
on has been just amazing.

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:02.540
 So we know Ned's arc
throughout these films.

00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:04.650
But what has been your
journey through this?

00:29:04.650 --> 00:29:06.270
 I feel like, I mean,
I've accomplished

00:29:06.270 --> 00:29:07.970
everything that I've wanted
to accomplish with Ned.

00:29:07.970 --> 00:29:09.803
I feel like he's definitely
become the guy in the chair

00:29:09.803 --> 00:29:10.980
to like in the action.

00:29:10.980 --> 00:29:13.280
So I think in that way,
he's had a great time.

00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:14.150
So, yeah.

00:29:14.150 --> 00:29:16.650
 If you can have any
Spider-Man gadget in real life,

00:29:16.650 --> 00:29:17.690
what would you choose?

00:29:17.690 --> 00:29:19.980
 Probably the webbed
wings so I can fly.

00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:20.780
 That's awesome.

00:29:20.780 --> 00:29:22.340
Jacob, thank you so much.
Enjoy the movie.

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:23.140
Thank you.

00:29:38.280 --> 00:29:39.090
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:41.700
We're here with JK Simmons
who plays J. Jonah Jameson.

00:29:41.700 --> 00:29:45.450
What was it like to come back
for this Spider-Man film?

00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:48.630
 Always a pleasure,
whatever incarnation--

00:29:48.630 --> 00:29:51.930
I hope they keep
reincarnating JJJ.

00:29:51.930 --> 00:29:54.240
 Now what's the difference
between this J. Jonah Jameson

00:29:54.240 --> 00:29:55.620
and the one you
played previously?

00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:58.140
 Only the hair really.

00:29:58.140 --> 00:30:00.090
 So this film is so massive.

00:30:00.090 --> 00:30:02.820
What was it like working with
this incredible ensemble?

00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:04.770
 Well, I'll tell
you, I was in and out.

00:30:04.770 --> 00:30:08.290
I still haven't met 2/3
of the cast of this movie.

00:30:08.290 --> 00:30:10.260
I'm hoping I get that
opportunity tonight.

00:30:10.260 --> 00:30:12.180
 So who are you
excited to see tonight?

00:30:12.180 --> 00:30:14.020
 That kid who plays Spider-Man,
whatever his name is--

00:30:14.020 --> 00:30:14.820
JOSH SALEH: What?

00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:19.030
 --and, you know,
the 75 bad guys,

00:30:19.030 --> 00:30:21.180
some of whom are, you
know, old leftovers

00:30:21.180 --> 00:30:22.827
like myself and some new ones.

00:30:22.827 --> 00:30:24.060
 Throughout your
Spider-Man journey,

00:30:24.060 --> 00:30:25.890
do you have a favorite moment?

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:27.960
 Can't pick one, not
going to even try.

00:30:43.340 --> 00:30:44.180
 What's up, Marvel fans?

00:30:44.180 --> 00:30:46.190
We're here with Jon Favreau,
who plays Happy Hogan.

00:30:46.190 --> 00:30:48.140
Now you started
the MCU directing

00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:49.580
Marvel Studios' Iron Man.

00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:51.620
What is it like to continue
that legacy of Iron Man

00:30:51.620 --> 00:30:52.520
as Happy Hogan?

00:30:52.520 --> 00:30:54.860
 Well, I love being a
part of this as an actor

00:30:54.860 --> 00:30:57.380
because I get to continue
to work with the people

00:30:57.380 --> 00:31:00.020
that I work with on
the Iron Man films.

00:31:00.020 --> 00:31:02.810
Also even before I
started directing,

00:31:02.810 --> 00:31:05.270
I remember visiting the
set of Spider-Man 3.

00:31:05.270 --> 00:31:07.230
That was my first experience.

00:31:07.230 --> 00:31:10.340
So it's nice that it's
all coming together.

00:31:10.340 --> 00:31:13.280
And I'm just happy that I've
been able to be a part of it

00:31:13.280 --> 00:31:15.990
in one way or another
for decades now.

00:31:15.990 --> 00:31:16.790
 That's awesome.

00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:18.950
Now that the entire world
knows who Spider-Man

00:31:18.950 --> 00:31:21.500
is, how does that affect Happy?

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:24.380
 Well, you know, Happy has
always been in on the secret

00:31:24.380 --> 00:31:27.980
with Tony Stark,
with Peter Parker.

00:31:27.980 --> 00:31:31.310
So Happy was always good at
being a professional wingman

00:31:31.310 --> 00:31:33.770
to help out and
help them navigate

00:31:33.770 --> 00:31:35.390
their way through
all the challenges

00:31:35.390 --> 00:31:37.490
of being a superhero.

00:31:37.490 --> 00:31:40.760
I think he offers a
lot of moral support.

00:31:40.760 --> 00:31:42.500
I don't think he's too
good for protection,

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.750
even though he's supposed
to be head of security.

00:31:44.750 --> 00:31:46.160
But I think he's a good friend.

00:31:46.160 --> 00:31:49.790
And I think for Peter
Parker, he was a good,

00:31:49.790 --> 00:31:51.230
I think he took it
upon himself to look

00:31:51.230 --> 00:31:53.480
after him after Tony was gone.

00:31:53.480 --> 00:31:55.460
So I really liked
playing that part.

00:31:55.460 --> 00:31:57.230
And I really like
Tom Holland a lot.

00:31:57.230 --> 00:32:01.160
And I loved popping onto
the set and working with Jon

00:32:01.160 --> 00:32:03.020
Watts and everybody there.

00:32:03.020 --> 00:32:04.700
It's a great group
of young actors.

00:32:04.700 --> 00:32:06.440
And as an actor, I love it.

00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:08.400
And I think it comes
through in the character.

00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:09.200
 That's awesome.

00:32:09.200 --> 00:32:11.690
Now do you have a favorite
MCU moment in Spider-Man

00:32:11.690 --> 00:32:13.160
through your journey?

00:32:13.160 --> 00:32:15.620
 Oh, in Spider-Man, I like
when we're in the bathroom,

00:32:15.620 --> 00:32:18.470
I think we were in
the bathroom together

00:32:18.470 --> 00:32:20.180
where I'm trying to
be like Nick Fury

00:32:20.180 --> 00:32:22.010
popping into his high school.

00:32:22.010 --> 00:32:25.030
And I confronted him.

00:32:25.030 --> 00:32:26.750
And someone flushes the toilet.

00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:30.710
So my really cool like Nick Fury
moment is completely undermined

00:32:30.710 --> 00:32:33.680
by a toilet flushing.

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:35.287
Yeah, I like that one a lot.

00:32:35.287 --> 00:32:36.420
 Awesome, Jon,
thank you so much.

00:32:36.420 --> 00:32:37.490
Enjoy the movie.
Thank you.

00:32:37.490 --> 00:32:38.290
 Have a good one.

00:32:53.460 --> 00:32:54.600
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:56.813
We're here with Willem Dafoe
who plays Green Goblin.

00:32:56.813 --> 00:32:58.380
All right, what was your
reaction when you were

00:32:58.380 --> 00:33:01.110
told the premise of this film?

00:33:01.110 --> 00:33:04.020
 Sounded good, good
enough to sign on,

00:33:04.020 --> 00:33:06.750
you know, to revisit
this character.

00:33:06.750 --> 00:33:08.410
 Now what was it like
revisiting that character?

00:33:08.410 --> 00:33:09.210
How was that?

00:33:09.210 --> 00:33:10.010
 It was great.

00:33:10.010 --> 00:33:13.500
I mean, it's-- yeah,
it's a continuation.

00:33:13.500 --> 00:33:16.170
And this is probably
the most ambitious

00:33:16.170 --> 00:33:18.570
filming of the series so far.

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:22.050
So it was great to be a part
of it, see some old friends,

00:33:22.050 --> 00:33:23.710
see some new friends, you know?

00:33:23.710 --> 00:33:24.510
 That's incredible.

00:33:24.510 --> 00:33:25.910
What was it like working
with Director Jon

00:33:25.910 --> 00:33:27.040
Watts and the awesome ensemble.

00:33:27.040 --> 00:33:27.840
 He was great.

00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:31.890
I mean, you know,
a lot of the people

00:33:31.890 --> 00:33:33.240
had worked together before.

00:33:33.240 --> 00:33:35.040
So they really
had good chemistry

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:37.170
already and a lot of trust.

00:33:37.170 --> 00:33:40.680
And, yeah, it was fun to work.

00:33:40.680 --> 00:33:44.550
You know, very loose, but
also, you know, we were

00:33:44.550 --> 00:33:46.560
making our days and having fun.

00:33:46.560 --> 00:33:49.920
 Do you have a favorite
Spider-Man moment in the MCU?

00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:52.140
 Oh, god, that's a tough one.

00:33:52.140 --> 00:33:54.090
 Yeah, too hard
again, there's so many.

00:33:54.090 --> 00:33:56.235
 You know, I enjoy
doing the action stuff.

00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:16.179
 Marvel fans, I am here with
Jamie Foxx, who plays Electro.

00:34:16.179 --> 00:34:18.020
What is it like returning
to this character

00:34:18.020 --> 00:34:18.820
after all this time?

00:34:18.820 --> 00:34:21.010
 It's been amazing, man,
like to be able to reboot

00:34:21.010 --> 00:34:24.040
the character and new
look, new vibe, and my kids

00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:26.070
here with me
representing Electro.

00:34:26.070 --> 00:34:27.920
They got the shoes
to represent Electro.

00:34:27.920 --> 00:34:28.900
They got the shoes.

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:30.489
So we've just been--
you know, just

00:34:30.489 --> 00:34:32.170
been happy to be on
this ride and can't wait

00:34:32.170 --> 00:34:33.730
for the world to see the movie.

00:34:33.730 --> 00:34:35.350
 What's different
about Electro this time?

00:34:35.350 --> 00:34:37.020
 Well, the way he
looks, right off the bat,

00:34:37.020 --> 00:34:37.820
it's a different look.

00:34:37.820 --> 00:34:42.100
He's simplified, potent,
kind of got a flyness to him.

00:34:42.100 --> 00:34:44.710
And so everybody
online has been really

00:34:44.710 --> 00:34:46.100
like reacting well to it.

00:34:46.100 --> 00:34:48.130
So just can't wait for
people to check it out.

00:34:48.130 --> 00:34:50.020
 I heard you brought
your own flavor to it.

00:34:50.020 --> 00:34:52.239
 Yeah, yeah, you know, you
got to bring your flavor to it.

00:34:52.239 --> 00:34:54.790
So, you know, the fact that
they were allowing, you know,

00:34:54.790 --> 00:34:57.500
accommodating with that makes
the whole movie feel better.

00:34:57.500 --> 00:34:58.300
Yeah.

00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:00.040
 Well, I'm excited to see it.

00:35:00.040 --> 00:35:02.050
What's the best part about
playing a super villain?

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:03.880
 Oh, it's always
good to be a bad guy.

00:35:03.880 --> 00:35:05.980
It's good being bad,
you know what I mean?

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:07.570
So it's like you're
doing Electro,

00:35:07.570 --> 00:35:09.410
there's so many layers when
you're a super villain,

00:35:09.410 --> 00:35:10.210
you know what I mean?

00:35:10.210 --> 00:35:12.220
So I can't wait for
you to check that out.

00:35:27.620 --> 00:35:28.530
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:35:28.530 --> 00:35:30.000
We're here with Kevin Feige.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.220
This is a huge
undertaking of a film.

00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:34.350
Where did you start?

00:35:34.350 --> 00:35:35.880
 We started at
the ending of Far

00:35:35.880 --> 00:35:37.650
From Home where we
knew that we had

00:35:37.650 --> 00:35:41.190
put Peter Parker in a very
hard circumstance where

00:35:41.190 --> 00:35:42.780
his identity was revealed.

00:35:42.780 --> 00:35:45.780
And from there, we
decide what happens next.

00:35:45.780 --> 00:35:47.730
And how do we make
things harder for him?

00:35:47.730 --> 00:35:49.150
He's been to space.

00:35:49.150 --> 00:35:50.940
He's become Spider-Man.

00:35:50.940 --> 00:35:52.440
He's lost his mentor.

00:35:52.440 --> 00:35:54.090
And now his identity
is revealed.

00:35:54.090 --> 00:35:56.490
And all he wants to do
is graduate high school

00:35:56.490 --> 00:35:57.540
and go to college.

00:35:57.540 --> 00:35:58.920
And we started there.

00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:01.510
 And the good old
Parker luck kicked in.

00:36:01.510 --> 00:36:04.090
You brought supervillains in
from previous spider-man movies

00:36:04.090 --> 00:36:04.890
into this.

00:36:04.890 --> 00:36:06.450
What was that process like?

00:36:06.450 --> 00:36:07.780
 It was very emotional.

00:36:07.780 --> 00:36:09.060
It always starts
with the place of,

00:36:09.060 --> 00:36:10.230
what do we think would be fun?

00:36:10.230 --> 00:36:11.830
What do we think would be cool?

00:36:11.830 --> 00:36:15.390
I've been making movies
for 20 years now at Marvel.

00:36:15.390 --> 00:36:18.480
And they started at this very
theater, as a matter of fact,

00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:21.210
with the premiere of Sam
Raimi's Spider-Man 1.

00:36:21.210 --> 00:36:23.220
And we were sitting
around a room

00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:26.550
and saying, if I saw Willem
Dafoe, who you just talked to,

00:36:26.550 --> 00:36:28.560
as Green Goblin again
and Alfred Molina,

00:36:28.560 --> 00:36:30.570
who's not able to be
here tonight, as Doc Ock,

00:36:30.570 --> 00:36:32.070
I would lose my mind.

00:36:32.070 --> 00:36:36.660
Just that starting
point and a lot of luck

00:36:36.660 --> 00:36:38.910
came together that
they were interested,

00:36:38.910 --> 00:36:40.200
we were able to bring them back.

00:36:40.200 --> 00:36:41.500
 Oh that's incredible.

00:36:41.500 --> 00:36:43.980
I can't wait to see
this incredible film.

00:36:43.980 --> 00:36:46.140
What are you most
proud of throughout

00:36:46.140 --> 00:36:47.550
the Spider-Man films?

00:36:47.550 --> 00:36:49.680
 Well I'm proud of
the collaboration we've

00:36:49.680 --> 00:36:51.900
had with Jon Watts
on three movies

00:36:51.900 --> 00:36:54.180
with Tom Holland on
three of his own movies,

00:36:54.180 --> 00:36:55.620
plus the Avengers movies.

00:36:55.620 --> 00:36:58.980
The entire relationship between
Sony and Marvel and Disney

00:36:58.980 --> 00:37:01.320
is really unprecedented
in Hollywood history.

00:37:01.320 --> 00:37:03.660
And it's all because
everybody loves Spider-Man.

00:37:03.660 --> 00:37:05.190
And that is amazing.

00:37:05.190 --> 00:37:06.680
I hope it shows in all
the movies as well.

00:37:06.680 --> 00:37:08.280
 Well, you said that
everyone loves Spider-Man.

00:37:08.280 --> 00:37:10.840
What makes him so
lovable and relatable.

00:37:10.840 --> 00:37:12.210
 I think that was
the genius of what

00:37:12.210 --> 00:37:14.190
Steve Ditko and Stan Lee
did all those years ago

00:37:14.190 --> 00:37:15.540
was they made him us.

00:37:15.540 --> 00:37:17.350
They made him
flawed and related.

00:37:17.350 --> 00:37:20.190
And, again, here he is in
this giant anticipated movie

00:37:20.190 --> 00:37:22.200
that may or may not
have consequences

00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:23.070
for the multiverse.

00:37:23.070 --> 00:37:25.380
But Peter Parker just
wants to go to college.

00:37:25.380 --> 00:37:27.090
Peter Parker just wants
to graduate high school.

00:37:27.090 --> 00:37:29.020
That's it.

00:37:29.020 --> 00:37:32.610
And you want to root
for that person.

00:37:32.610 --> 00:37:34.200
 Kevin, thank you so much.
Enjoy the movie.

00:37:34.200 --> 00:37:35.580
Thank you so much.
Have a good night.

00:37:35.580 --> 00:37:36.380
Thank you.

00:37:51.470 --> 00:37:53.940
 Marvel fans, I am here
with Zendaya, MJ herself.

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:55.050
How are you?
- I'm good.

00:37:55.050 --> 00:37:55.850
How are you?

00:37:55.850 --> 00:37:57.050
 I'm doing pretty great.

00:37:57.050 --> 00:37:58.290
So I have a couple of questions.

00:37:58.290 --> 00:38:00.140
This is the biggest
Spider-Man film yet

00:38:00.140 --> 00:38:01.790
and there's a lot of stunts.

00:38:01.790 --> 00:38:04.460
How did it feel to be a web
slinging and flying high?

00:38:04.460 --> 00:38:06.000
 Oh, man, it was so much fun.

00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:07.560
I loved being able
to do that stuff,

00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:09.300
especially because we
feel incredibly safe.

00:38:09.300 --> 00:38:10.880
We have an amazing
stunt coordinator.

00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:14.030
And you just get to have fun.

00:38:14.030 --> 00:38:15.930
I'm not afraid of
heights in that way.

00:38:15.930 --> 00:38:17.780
So I feel really good about it.

00:38:17.780 --> 00:38:18.920
 Well, I can't wait to see.

00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:21.500
How has MJ changed
since we last seen her?

00:38:21.500 --> 00:38:22.940
 I think she's just
opening up more.

00:38:22.940 --> 00:38:27.230
I think now that she has Peter
in her life and someone--

00:38:27.230 --> 00:38:30.740
and Ned, obviously, people who
feel that love her for who she

00:38:30.740 --> 00:38:33.140
is, I think she's
able to slightly just

00:38:33.140 --> 00:38:34.910
open up a little bit
more and maybe even

00:38:34.910 --> 00:38:35.990
be a little bit more positive.

00:38:35.990 --> 00:38:38.123
Because usually she's like
the nihilistic friend, right?

00:38:38.123 --> 00:38:39.290
She's the one that's
always looking

00:38:39.290 --> 00:38:40.620
at things glass half empty.

00:38:40.620 --> 00:38:42.230
So it's nice to see
that side of her.

00:38:58.050 --> 00:38:58.860
 Hello Marvel fans.

00:38:58.860 --> 00:39:00.060
We're here with
Benedict Cumberbatch

00:39:00.060 --> 00:39:01.020
who plays Doctor Strange.

00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:03.370
You have had quite the
busy life, my friend.

00:39:03.370 --> 00:39:04.170
 Yep.

00:39:04.170 --> 00:39:07.140
 What is it like to dive
into the Marvel multiverse?

00:39:07.140 --> 00:39:10.830
 Marvel is a fun place to be
right now as Doctor Strange.

00:39:10.830 --> 00:39:11.850
That's all I will say.

00:39:11.850 --> 00:39:15.300
And, yeah, you know,
he brings something

00:39:15.300 --> 00:39:17.640
very interesting to this film.

00:39:17.640 --> 00:39:20.130
But most of all, having worked
with Tom-- not just on this,

00:39:20.130 --> 00:39:22.050
but on a couple of other
projects-- it's just,

00:39:22.050 --> 00:39:24.570
it's just wonderful to be by his
side again and doing what we do

00:39:24.570 --> 00:39:27.570
and establishing and maturing
and growing that relationship.

00:39:27.570 --> 00:39:28.470
It's fantastic.

00:39:28.470 --> 00:39:30.000
 What is it like
bringing Dr. Strange

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.460
into the world of Spider-Man?

00:39:32.460 --> 00:39:34.060
 A lot of fun, a lot of fun.

00:39:34.060 --> 00:39:36.670
You know, I get to play the
grown-up surrounded by kids.

00:39:36.670 --> 00:39:37.470
I could say that.

00:39:37.470 --> 00:39:38.270
They're half my age.

00:39:38.270 --> 00:39:39.150
They are kids.

00:39:39.150 --> 00:39:40.770
I'm blown away by
their professionalism,

00:39:40.770 --> 00:39:42.180
by the atmosphere
they create on set,

00:39:42.180 --> 00:39:44.070
by the fun that is
to be on that set.

00:39:44.070 --> 00:39:46.470
Jon Watts is a
phenomenal director.

00:39:46.470 --> 00:39:48.540
He's such a joy to work with.

00:39:48.540 --> 00:39:49.740
He's great on the granular.

00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:51.870
He gives you context to
understand where your place is

00:39:51.870 --> 00:39:53.490
in the story and the
development of it,

00:39:53.490 --> 00:39:55.080
even when all the story
hasn't been finished,

00:39:55.080 --> 00:39:56.780
which is often the way with
these films at the time

00:39:56.780 --> 00:39:57.930
of production starting.

00:39:57.930 --> 00:40:00.660
And it is just fun
from start to finish.

00:40:00.660 --> 00:40:02.760
 What goes through
Dr. Strange's mind.

00:40:02.760 --> 00:40:04.980
After saving worlds
and universes,

00:40:04.980 --> 00:40:07.000
a young Peter Parker
comes up saying, hey,

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:09.070
can you craft a spell
to have people forget?

00:40:09.070 --> 00:40:11.070
 I think the first thing that
goes through his mind, as you

00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:13.260
see in the film, is like, yeah,
sure, I want to help you out,

00:40:13.260 --> 00:40:14.490
kid.
You did great back there.

00:40:14.490 --> 00:40:16.890
And you're one of them
and us and, you know,

00:40:16.890 --> 00:40:18.580
we're doing-- we're all
on the same team here.

00:40:18.580 --> 00:40:20.670
So, sure, I'll
help a friend out.

00:40:20.670 --> 00:40:22.770
It doesn't really take
into account that he's

00:40:22.770 --> 00:40:24.660
still a kid at high school.

00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:28.170
And in trying to
people please or going,

00:40:28.170 --> 00:40:31.110
yeah, OK, let's do one
for the team, yeah,

00:40:31.110 --> 00:40:34.410
some crazy stuff is unleashed.

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.060
And that's where
the relationship

00:40:36.060 --> 00:40:37.890
starts to evolve and
mature and that's

00:40:37.890 --> 00:40:38.910
what I'm really excited about.

00:40:38.910 --> 00:40:40.950
I mean, there's
some crazy reveals

00:40:40.950 --> 00:40:42.510
and fun spills and
thrills in this.

00:40:42.510 --> 00:40:45.990
But also, for me as an actor,
the thing that matters most

00:40:45.990 --> 00:40:48.480
is that emotional
connection to a character

00:40:48.480 --> 00:40:50.800
and the people who
surround him and the world

00:40:50.800 --> 00:40:51.600
that surrounds him.

00:40:51.600 --> 00:40:54.730
So with Tom and I, that's a
really beautiful relationship

00:40:54.730 --> 00:40:55.530
that's kicking off.

00:41:10.850 --> 00:41:11.720
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:41:11.720 --> 00:41:13.760
We are here with Tom Holland
who plays Peter Parker.

00:41:13.760 --> 00:41:16.550
This is one of the biggest
Spider-Man films ever made.

00:41:16.550 --> 00:41:19.130
What was your reaction
when you read the premise?

00:41:19.130 --> 00:41:20.370
 Oh, man, I was blown away.

00:41:20.370 --> 00:41:22.100
I was also so skeptical.

00:41:22.100 --> 00:41:23.510
At the time, I was
like, there's no way

00:41:23.510 --> 00:41:24.510
that they could pull this off.

00:41:24.510 --> 00:41:26.330
There's no way that
they'll be able to bring

00:41:26.330 --> 00:41:29.780
these villains back into
this universe and make sense.

00:41:29.780 --> 00:41:30.590
But they did.

00:41:30.590 --> 00:41:32.360
And they've done it in
a wonderful fashion.

00:41:32.360 --> 00:41:35.060
The movie is incredibly
heartfelt. It's funny.

00:41:35.060 --> 00:41:36.110
It's emotional.

00:41:36.110 --> 00:41:37.310
It's exciting.

00:41:37.310 --> 00:41:39.530
And, you know, Jon
Watts has really

00:41:39.530 --> 00:41:40.460
knocked it out of the park.

00:41:40.460 --> 00:41:43.130
So to be here tonight
celebrating this movie,

00:41:43.130 --> 00:41:46.130
I honestly cannot even begin
to explain to you how happy

00:41:46.130 --> 00:41:47.330
I am and how excited I am.

00:41:47.330 --> 00:41:49.910
If you had told me 10 years
ago that you'll be playing

00:41:49.910 --> 00:41:51.950
Spider-Man in a movie like
this, I would have been like,

00:41:51.950 --> 00:41:53.870
you're a liar.

00:41:53.870 --> 00:41:55.827
 Well, in a movie
like this, exactly.

00:41:55.827 --> 00:41:56.660
Look at all these people.

00:41:56.660 --> 00:41:57.500
They love you.

00:41:57.500 --> 00:42:00.080
Movie like this, you're
playing opposite super villains

00:42:00.080 --> 00:42:01.430
from previous Spider-Man movies.

00:42:01.430 --> 00:42:02.750
What is that like?

00:42:02.750 --> 00:42:03.620
 It's incredible.

00:42:03.620 --> 00:42:07.190
I mean, I've been a huge fan of
these movies since I was a kid.

00:42:07.190 --> 00:42:08.610
I remember seeing
Tobey's movies.

00:42:08.610 --> 00:42:10.050
I remember seeing
Andrew's movies.

00:42:10.050 --> 00:42:12.890
So to get the chance to share
the screen with their villains

00:42:12.890 --> 00:42:17.000
has been one of the most
rewarding aspects of my career.

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:19.200
And I'm so lucky
to be here tonight.

00:42:19.200 --> 00:42:20.870
I can't wait to share
the night with them.

00:42:20.870 --> 00:42:23.690
And I'm seeing Tom Rothman over
there, my boss, who I love.

00:42:23.690 --> 00:42:24.680
He's been so kind to me.

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:26.330
I want to go and
give him a big hug.

00:42:26.330 --> 00:42:29.450
And, honestly, I
am beyond excited.

00:42:29.450 --> 00:42:31.970
 Peter goes through so much,
the death of Tony Stark,

00:42:31.970 --> 00:42:34.640
Mysterio letting him know
that his entire identity, what

00:42:34.640 --> 00:42:36.570
is that like for Peter
Parker in this film?

00:42:36.570 --> 00:42:37.370
 It's tough.

00:42:37.370 --> 00:42:39.500
I mean, everyone's been
asking me in the press,

00:42:39.500 --> 00:42:42.350
can you relate to it
because you're famous?

00:42:42.350 --> 00:42:44.900
But I'm famous for making
movies and he's famous for being

00:42:44.900 --> 00:42:46.010
a mass murderer.

00:42:46.010 --> 00:42:47.690
So it's slightly different.

00:42:47.690 --> 00:42:50.240
But it's been a very
exciting challenge, something

00:42:50.240 --> 00:42:51.920
I've really enjoyed
taking on, bringing

00:42:51.920 --> 00:42:53.300
to life in the character.

00:42:53.300 --> 00:42:55.640
It definitely totally
shifts the movie.

00:42:55.640 --> 00:42:58.410
It makes the movie feel very
different to the previous two,

00:42:58.410 --> 00:42:59.210
which is great.

00:42:59.210 --> 00:43:00.010
I love change.

00:43:00.010 --> 00:43:01.170
And I love this movie.

00:43:01.170 --> 00:43:02.390
And I love everyone here.

00:43:02.390 --> 00:43:03.790
And it's awesome.

00:43:03.790 --> 00:43:05.540
 Tom, you've got a busy night.
Enjoy the premiere.

00:43:05.540 --> 00:43:06.800
Thank you so much.
Thank you.

00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:07.895
- Thank you so much.
- Have a good one.

00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:30.260
 Oh, that was amazing.

00:43:30.260 --> 00:43:33.110
 It was incredible-- so many
talented actors, the cast,

00:43:33.110 --> 00:43:35.020
the crew, I'm speechless.

00:43:35.020 --> 00:43:36.970
 As am I. Let us know what
your favorite interview

00:43:36.970 --> 00:43:38.093
was in the comments below.

